Fix MSVC compilation of headers-more-nginx-module.

nginx's win32 build compiles with a precompiled header
(-Yungx_config.h): cl discards everything in a translation unit before
the #include <ngx_config.h> line. headers-more includes ngx_config.h
first inside ddebug.h, so each .c file's DDEBUG define (and everything
else preceding the include chain) was silently thrown away, breaking
the build. Move ngx_config.h after the DDEBUG define in each .c file
and last among the nginx includes in ddebug.h.

Based on the technique from
https://github.com/ewwink/headers-more-nginx-module-for-windows
(which reorders the includes inside the .c files; this variant adds
ngx_config.h before ddebug.h and drops the stray later include — a
cleaner equivalent). headers-more-nginx-module is BSD-2-Clause.

git apply ignores everything above the first "diff --git" line, so
this prose travels with the patch.

diff --git a/src/ddebug.h b/src/ddebug.h
index 13879af..6be37a7 100644
--- a/src/ddebug.h
+++ b/src/ddebug.h
@@ -2,10 +2,10 @@
 #define DDEBUG_H


-#include <ngx_config.h>
 #include <ngx_core.h>
 #include <ngx_http.h>
 #include <nginx.h>
+#include <ngx_config.h>


 #if defined(DDEBUG) && (DDEBUG)
diff --git a/src/ngx_http_headers_more_filter_module.c b/src/ngx_http_headers_more_filter_module.c
index 0bb6fec..26556b7 100644
--- a/src/ngx_http_headers_more_filter_module.c
+++ b/src/ngx_http_headers_more_filter_module.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #ifndef DDEBUG
 #define DDEBUG 0
 #endif
+#include <ngx_config.h>
 #include "ddebug.h"


@@ -14,7 +15,6 @@
 #include "ngx_http_headers_more_headers_out.h"
 #include "ngx_http_headers_more_headers_in.h"
 #include "ngx_http_headers_more_util.h"
-#include <ngx_config.h>


 /* config handlers */
